WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.520
We all like to imagine that our favorite actors
and actresses are great people in real life.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.990
Sure, they might play a jerk onscreen once
in awhile, but that's just acting, right?

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:10.990
It's what they do.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:16.250
Well, with great fame comes great entitlement,
and some of Hollywood's finest are just plain

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:17.580
nasty at times.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.920
Each of these actors have earned a bad rep
for the way they behave between takes, be

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:26.980
it talking down to craft services, warring
with co-stars, or fighting with directors.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.679
Maybe they were all just having a bad day
… over and over again.

00:00:30.679 --> 00:00:34.159
“Again and again, and again and again and
again.”

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:35.290
“Ahhhh!”

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:39.899
Here are a few of the big-name actors people
hate working with.

00:00:39.899 --> 00:00:41.039
Val Kilmer

00:00:41.039 --> 00:00:44.770
At this point, Val Kilmer's reputation precedes
him.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:49.020
As far as acting jerks go, Val Kilmer is right
at the top of the list.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:54.160
Starting all the way back in 1995 with Batman
Forever, Kilmer has been known for his attitude

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.160
when the cameras aren't rolling.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:01.250
After production, director Joel Schumacher
said in an interview that Val Kilmer was "childish

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:02.250
and impossible."

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:06.310
But his words were hardly that last we'd hear
of Kilmer's tough 'tude.

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:11.190
After The Island of Dr. Moreau hit theaters
the very next year, director John Frankenheimer

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:12.770
famously said, quote:

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:17.409
"I will never climb Mount Everest, and I will
never work with Val Kilmer again."

00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:18.409
End quote.

00:01:18.409 --> 00:01:22.619
Meanwhile, one of the movie's actors, Neil
Young, had this to say about his antics:

00:01:22.619 --> 00:01:26.860
“He was just kind of being a bit rude and
abrasive.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:30.229
Um, he...that was his character though, so
fair go.

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:35.430
Maybe that was the way he prepared to be an
a--hole, to, you know, act like one off camera.”

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:37.399
Noticing a pattern here?

00:01:37.399 --> 00:01:39.259
Alec Baldwin

00:01:39.259 --> 00:01:42.740
There's no doubting that Alec Baldwin is an
outspoken man.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:47.590
Whether he's being accused of fighting paparazzi,
shouting homophobic slurs, or calling his

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:52.149
own daughter names in a leaked voicemail,
his private life has a way of being shoved

00:01:52.149 --> 00:01:54.659
into the limelight on a regular basis.

00:01:54.659 --> 00:01:58.350
As a number of his co-stars have said, that's
just who he is.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:03.320
Shia LaBeouf, who's had no shortage of conflicts
all his own — more on that in a minute — famously

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:09.920
left the Broadway show Orphans in 2013 because
the two actors had clashed so often at rehearsals.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:14.410
And on 30 Rock, his co-star Cheyenne Jackson
had one thing to say about Baldwin.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:20.000
Quote: "What I learned from him was really
good comedic timing and don't get in his light."

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.480
End quote.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:22.960
Shia LaBeouf

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:27.860
For a guy who got his start playing the adorable
lead in Disney's Even Stevens, Shia LaBeouf

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:31.590
sure has shed any presumption of innocence
in the years since.

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:36.190
LaBeouf made his way to the big screen in
a big way shortly after the show ended, with

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:41.890
major blockbusters like Constantine, I, Robot,
and, of course, the Transformers franchise,

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:44.800
which kicked his career straight into the
stratosphere.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.570
After he reached such great heights, though,
things changed very quickly — and bizarrely.

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:54.770
Shia started taking more avant garde roles
and staged a bunch of strange publicity stunts,

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:59.670
like wearing a paper bag that said "I am not
famous anymore" and filming himself watching

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:01.770
all of his own movies in a row.

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:06.600
Clearly, he wanted the world to take him seriously,
but his penchant for weird antics and over-the-top

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.730
method acting has begun to rub people the
wrong way.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:14.120
He's even gotten into fist fights with at
least two of his co-stars — with Tom Hardy

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:21.200
on the set of 2012's Lawless and again after
punching Brad Pitt on 2014's war epic Fury.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:24.950
In both cases, his co-stars let it slide where
the public was concerned.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:29.220
"Because Shia's got this weird little left
uppercut you've gotta stay away from him,

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:30.220
you gotta watch that one."

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:35.030
But the production on Lawless also saw LaBeouf
guzzling actual bottles of moonshine to get

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:39.280
into character and carving his name into Mia
Wasikowska's dressing room door.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:43.660
LaBeouf might not want to be famous anymore,
but he's quickly becoming infamous.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:44.660
“What does that mean?

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:45.400
Infamous?”

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.080
“Oh ho, Dusty.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:51.880
‘Infamous’ is, is when you’re MORE than
famous.”

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.610
Hmmm...not quite.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:56.440
But that reminds us…

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:57.450
Chevy Chase

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:02.470
His character history might read like a who's
who in likeable goofs, but Chevy Chase has

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:06.140
something of a reputation as one of the meanest
men in show biz.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:09.760
That rep has followed him all the way from
his rock star beginnings on Saturday Night

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:13.610
Live in the '70s up to his recent recurring
gig on Community.

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:17.340
Highlights from his worst moments include
getting into a fist fight with Bill Murray

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:23.010
and suggesting that former SNL co-star Terry
Sweeney, who was openly gay, do a weekly segment

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:27.460
where he would get weighed — to see if he
had contracted AIDS yet.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:29.120
“Oh sorry.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:30.220
Hi fellas.”

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:34.430
It certainly seems like Chevy Chase has a
penchant for rubbing people the wrong way.

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:39.660
He even came clean about it in 2012, when
he said, quote: "Nobody prepares you for what

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:42.510
happens when you get famous, and I didn't
handle it well."

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:43.660
End quote.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:46.930
That may be the understatement of the decade.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.940
Mandy Patinkin

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:53.290
He might not quite be a household name, but
you probably know his work from his unforgettable

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:56.410
role in 1987's The Princess Bride.

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:57.410
“Hello.

00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:59.930
My name is Inigo Montoya.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:02.580
You killed my father.

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:04.760
Prepare to die.”

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:09.660
More recently, you may have seen him in CBS's
Criminal Minds and the Golden Globe-winning

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.570
Showtime series Homeland.

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:16.040
With so much success in film and television,
people probably suspect that Mandy Patinkin

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:17.470
is a pretty nice guy.

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:21.030
But by his own admission, he can be extremely
difficult to work with.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:26.100
Before nearly destroying his television career
in 2007 by suddenly walking away from Criminal

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:31.030
Minds and never coming back, Patinkin was
already behaving like a stuck-up starlet.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:35.910
In a 2013 interview with the New York Times,
he came clean with his sordid past on the

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:36.980
set.

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:41.780
Talking about the hospital drama Chicago Hope,
Patinkin said, quote: "I never let directors

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:46.130
talk to me, because I was so spoiled … I
was saying, 'Don't talk to me, I don't want

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.130
your opinion.'

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:48.590
I behaved abominably."

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:49.590
End quote.

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:51.920
Hey, at least he can admit it.

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:54.020
Mike Myers

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:58.090
It's almost a cliche now that comedians often
have darker sides.

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:02.180
And Mike Myers isn't immune to the pressures
of being a full-time funnyman.

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:07.340
Between Wayne's World, Austin Powers, and
The Love Guru, Myers' whole brand is over-the-top,

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:11.610
outrageously colorful characters, most of
whom he's meticulously crafted himself.

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:14.370
"Throw me a frickin' bone here."

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:18.770
He's been called a perfectionist on his good
days, and on his worst he's been dubbed "emotionally

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:20.590
needy" and "difficult."

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:24.610
That characterization comes directly from
Penelope Spheeris, who directed Mike Myers

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.680
in 1992's Wayne's World.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:31.340
Spheeris also told the story of how Mike Myers
stormed off the set once because the caterers

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:33.290
didn't provide margarine for his bagel.

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:36.270
"You kiss your mother with that mouth?"

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:38.370
Gwyneth Paltrow

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:42.340
It's easy enough for the internet to hate
Gwyneth Paltrow, who's managed to outrage

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:47.000
non-millionaire parents everywhere with her
lifestyle blog "Goop" and has an unfortunate

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:49.710
tendency to come across as aloof and entitled.

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:54.360
As we hear all so often, Paltrow is just one
of those everyday moms, the kind who allegedly

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:59.510
refuses to touch "other people's shower water"
at her gym and won't use toilet paper if the

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:01.400
roll is already unwrapped.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:05.840
So yeah, her apparently uptight mannerisms
have earned her a starring role as a punching

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:07.520
bag for celebrity gossip.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:10.780
But she's also difficult to work with for
other A-listers, too.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:15.830
According to reports from the set of 2010's
Iron Man 2, Paltrow made it a point to avoid

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:19.970
her co-star Scarlett Johansson during the
whole production and then got angry when she

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:23.440
was upstaged by Johansson during the promotional
work for the film.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:27.410
Of course, one of her press representatives
denied those claims, so it's possible that

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:30.200
the story was simply another piece of trumped-up
gossip.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:33.850
But when it comes to Madame Goop, who can
tell?

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:35.370
Katherine Heigl

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:40.830
Few people have become the target of tabloid
fodder as completely as Katherine Heigl.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:45.430
In 2008, she publicly bashed her comedy breakout
film Knocked Up as "sexist," and she also

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:49.400
famously declined to be considered for the
Emmys because she thought the Grey's Anatomy

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:53.580
writers didn't give her enough "juicy, dramatic
material" to deserve a nomination.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:57.440
The series' creator, Shonda Rhimes, said afterward
of the situation:

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:01.530
“Yeah, on some level it stung and on some
level I was not surprised.”

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:02.530
“You weren’t.”

00:08:02.530 --> 00:08:03.030
“No.”

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:03.810
“Okay.

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:04.910
“When people say who they are, believe them.”

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:09.780
Rhimes reportedly declined an offer for Heigl
to return to the show after her character's

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:10.780
departure.

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:12.960
Patrick Dempsey

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:17.200
Katherine Heigl wasn't the only real-life
pill on the set of Grey's, either.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:21.770
Patrick Dempsey, better known as "McDreamy"
was also apparently suspended once for acting

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:26.010
"like a diva" on set and was killed off on
the show not long after that.

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:28.870
Dempsey had reportedly clashed with Shonda
Rhimes.

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:32.839
While he later denied that there was anything
but goodwill between him and the cast, that

00:08:32.839 --> 00:08:35.510
story has since been hard to shake.

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:37.469
Bruce Willis

00:08:37.469 --> 00:08:42.180
You may remember the time Kevin Smith described
Bruce Willis as "f—ing soul crushing" to

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:45.470
work with, after teaming with him for 2010's
Cop Out.

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:49.589
According to Smith, Bruce Willis was pretty
much his hero … until he actually worked

00:08:49.589 --> 00:08:50.589
with the guy.

00:08:50.589 --> 00:08:54.851
Meanwhile, Tears of the Sun director Antoine
Fuqua called Bruce Willis a major "pain in

00:08:54.851 --> 00:08:59.150
the ass" to work with, and Sylvester Stallone
seemed to have similar issues with Bruce Willis

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:01.100
during the Expendables series.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:06.050
He dropped Willis for Harrison Ford in Expendables
3, and immediately after announcing the switch,

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:11.279
he tweeted a vague, possible stab at Willis
that read, quote: "greedy and lazy … a sure

00:09:11.279 --> 00:09:13.160
formula for career failure."

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:14.529
End quote.

00:09:14.529 --> 00:09:16.010
Teri Hatcher

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:19.860
Desperate Housewives was as dramatic behind
the scenes as it was for at-home audiences.

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:25.470
The hot ABC show had trouble from the start,
and actress Teri Hatcher, who played Susan,

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:29.510
apparently took the brunt of the criticism
from her cast mates, who felt she acted like

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:30.510
a diva.

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:34.390
Hatcher's co-star Nicollette Sheridan went
so far as to call her the "meanest woman in

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:35.390
the world."

00:09:35.390 --> 00:09:39.640
After the final episode of Desperate Housewives,
Hatcher reportedly stated, quote: "I will

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:43.080
never disclose the true and complicated journey
of us all."

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:44.080
End quote.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:45.740
It's probably just as well.

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:48.980
Some questions are probably best left unanswered.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.360
Steven Seagal

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:53.360
This action star was basically born to raise
hell.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:57.480
And while he's no longer headlining big-budget
features, Steven Seagal is still churning

00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:01.830
out low-budget films left and right, even
though he's developed a reputation for not

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:03.550
being the best dude around.

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:07.610
Steven Seagal has been hit with countless
allegations of sexual assault, among other

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:12.350
charges, over the years, including one by
Under Siege 2 auditioner Jenny McCarthy, who

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:16.710
said in an interview that Seagal told her
to take off her dress during a private audition,

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:19.460
despite the absence of nudity in the film.

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:20.460
Yuck.

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:24.710
He's also been known to flex some of his silver-screened
might on his male co-stars when the cameras

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:25.710
weren't rolling.

00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:29.820
John Leguizamo reportedly claimed that Seagal
elbowed him up against a wall with maximum

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:34.960
conviction on the set of 1996's Executive
Decision, simply because Leguizamo laughed

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:38.640
at something Seagal said, thinking it was
a joke — when it wasn't.

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:43.900
“And he came up, and he...he Tae Kwon Do’d
my ass against a brick wall.

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:44.900
He went ptffhhh!

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:48.420
He’s six foot five and caught me off guard,
knocked all the air out of me.

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:50.000
I was like ‘hhhhhhuuu.’”

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:51.550
Thanks for watching!

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:54.540
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:57.220
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

